<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Wideband OFDM Beamforming for 5G : &lt;BR&gt;exploring RF Beamforming with Phased Arrays &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoBodyText style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This example&amp;nbsp;demonstrates TX Beamforming in&amp;nbsp;a 28.5 GHz OFDM link with&amp;nbsp;4 MIMO streams that is typical of 5G standards investigations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;The transmitter&apos;s RF beamforming is performed two different ways:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;U&gt;Folders 0,1&lt;/U&gt; - The TX array is modeled with nonlinear PA in the&amp;nbsp;Phased Array analysis, and brought to the system level using RF_LINK.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;U&gt;Folder 2&lt;/U&gt; - The TX beamformer is modeled in Dataflow using ideal gain/phase parts.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;You can compare the modeling approaches and the EVM results.&amp;nbsp; If you raise the power of the signal, or lower the distortion thresholds for the Phased Array PAs, you can observe the EVM degradation due to the additional RF impairments.&amp;nbsp; Also, if any of the 4 beams begin to overlap with each other, then there will also be some final EVM degradation.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;(You can change the PHI and THETA arrays to re-steer the beams, if you wish to explore this&amp;nbsp;source of self-interference from beamforming)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Additional 5G Notes: &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This 5G example can also be found in the \Examples\Baseband Ver.\5GAdvancedModem directory.&amp;nbsp; In that version, it uses more specific 5G parts from the special library.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The SystemVue 5G library supports a number of beamforming functions and modeling tasks:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Flexible beamforming structure, including full digital beamforming, hybrid beamforming and full RF/analog beamforming. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;OFDM MIMO transmission&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;RF impairments&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Taylor window for RF beamforming&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;antenna coupling&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;CCDF and spectrum measurement&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;TX 3D beam plotting for combined signal and each RF channel&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Custom beam pattern import with EMpro and HFSS formats&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;EVM measurement and constellation output&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;The parameters to configure the simulation are located in Equation Tab of&amp;nbsp;Design1&amp;nbsp;with the following categories.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;&#x00B7;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT: 7pt &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;System configuration&lt;/STRONG&gt;: set key parameters for the whole system, including central frequency, sample rate, power and RF chains. Also users can set desired beam direction for each RF chains.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;&#x00B7;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT: 7pt &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Antenna array configuration&lt;/STRONG&gt;: define antenna array structure and the mapping from RF chains to antennas.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;&#x00B7;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT: 7pt &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Impairment analysis&lt;/STRONG&gt;: set the impairments in antenna array, RF power amplifiers.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt 0.5in; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;&#x00B7;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT: 7pt &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;OFDM source configuration&lt;/STRONG&gt;: configure OFDM MIMO source&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;It is suggested to change parameters in &lt;STRONG&gt;System configuration&lt;/STRONG&gt;, &lt;STRONG&gt;Antenna array configuration&lt;/STRONG&gt; and &lt;STRONG&gt;Impairment analysis &lt;/STRONG&gt;per system configuration, and leave the parameter in &lt;STRONG&gt;OFDM source configuration &lt;/STRONG&gt;unchanged for OFDM MIMO source if there is no need to change OFDM signals.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Upon the settings, users will see &lt;STRONG&gt;NumOfRFChains&lt;/STRONG&gt; beams in the combined signal, the beam directions of which depend on &lt;STRONG&gt;Theta&lt;/STRONG&gt; and &lt;STRONG&gt;Phi&lt;/STRONG&gt; defined in the equation page&amp;nbsp;of the schematic. The EVM is measured accordingly.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;Notes: &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo2&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;1.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT: 7pt &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;For antenna array, ULA (uniform&amp;nbsp;linear array) and UPA (uniform planar array)&amp;nbsp;arrays are supported. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt 0.5in; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo2&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;mso-list: Ignore&quot;&gt;2.&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT: 7pt &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;For antenna pattern predefined for three sector antenna when &lt;STRONG&gt;AntennaPatternType &lt;/STRONG&gt;=&lt;STRONG&gt; Three Sector Antenna for Y-Z URA&lt;/STRONG&gt;, the generated antenna pattern towards x-axis which is consistent with the assumption of antenna array in Y-Z plane.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt 0.5in; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo2&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;3.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 11pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Calibri&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-fareast-font-family: SimSun; mso-bidi-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: ZH-CN; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;As a result, to have custom antenna pattern work properly, it is expected that custom 3D antenna beam&amp;nbsp;pattern towards x-axis when&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt;AntennaPatternType&lt;/STRONG&gt; = &lt;STRONG&gt;Pattern File&lt;/STRONG&gt;.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 8pt 0.5in; TEXT-INDENT: -0.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo2&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 11pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Calibri&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-fareast-font-family: SimSun; mso-bidi-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: ZH-CN; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=Arial&gt;4.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; For EVM measurement, the default receiver beamforming is optimal&amp;nbsp;as the recevier beams (defined by RxTheta and RxPhi in Equations Tab) are exactly pointed to transmit beam directions. Users can change these two values if reveiver beamforming is not ideal.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 11pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Calibri&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; LINE-HEIGHT: 107%; mso-fareast-font-family: SimSun; mso-bidi-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: ZH-CN; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;</Text>
